# Runtime payloads that are not libretro cores.
#
# cores.list carries one .so per line, dropped into cores/. Some systems need
# more than that: the 3D engine is a whole LOVE runtime plus its game archive,
# and its mod is a zip the app unpacks itself. Those land under data/ instead,
# which is where WinNative already looks for Dolphin's and ARMSX2's runtime
# files.
#
# fork repo|release asset|destination under data/|unzip or copy
#
#   unzip  the archive is expanded into the destination directory
#   copy   the asset is placed in the destination directory as-is, because
#          something on the device expects the archive itself
#
# Every entry also joins the freshness fingerprint, so a new engine or mod
# build rebuilds the bundle just as a new core does.

# The Gen 1 3D engine: arm64 LOVE runtime + game.love. WinNative loads these by
# absolute path out of the bundle, so the layout inside the zip (game.love and
# lib/*.so) is what it expects to find here.
gen1recomp|gen1recomp-engine.zip|gen1recomp|unzip

# The 3D voxel mod. Kept as a zip on purpose: WinNative unpacks it into the
# engine's own mod directory at launch, because files written there by anything
# other than the app itself are not fully readable by it.
DramaticShapeVoxelMod|DRAMATIC_SHAPE.zip|gen1recomp-mods|copy
